body:
Tier: 3

Found in adversarial review pass pass-1 reconciliation (lever-12) at `60f4ad89`, root-cause group LP4: P1G-02.

## P1G-02

- finder: P1G
- location: `pgpm_core/install.sql:8238`
- lens: pass-1 reconciliation
- tier: 3
- scenario: pass-1 R8: regrain_history picks the smallest-lo attached child with no coarseness filter, so after one hierarchical pass it raises 'the target step does not subdivide its range' on an already-fine child while a coarse child remains; it should regrain the oldest coarse child, as the guide and reference say
- root cause (verifier): regrain_history picks the smallest-lo attached child with no 'the target subdivides it' filter (maintain's auto-regrain selection has one), so after a hierarchical pass it raises 'the target step does not subdivide its range' on an already-fine child while a coarse child remains; docs/guide.md says it regrains 'the oldest coarse child' and recommends it for hierarchical splits ('pgpm.regrain()/regrain_history() ... stay fully general'). Refuses where the documented contract says it acts; no data at risk, regrain(parent, child) is the workaround.

Reproduction: `repro.sql`, the finder's, run unchanged by the verifier.

```sql
-- P1G-02 (pass-1 R8): regrain_history picks the smallest-lo attached child with no coarseness filter.
-- docs/guide.md: "regrain_history regrains the oldest coarse child (the monolith)", and for a hierarchical
-- split "drive it by hand with pgpm.regrain()/regrain_history() instead -- those stay fully general".
-- Present: after monolith -> 50-wide -> (first 50-wide child) -> 10-wide, the next regrain_history call
-- raises nosubdiv against the fine [0,10) while the coarse [50,100) is still there. Absent: it splits
-- [50,100).
create extension if not exists pgtap;
set client_min_messages = warning;
select plan(6);

create table public.r8 (id bigint primary key, body text);
insert into public.r8 select g, 'row ' || g from generate_series(1, 95) g;
call pgpm.transmute('public.r8', 'id', 10::bigint, p_obtain => 3);
insert into public.r8 values (105, 'frontier');           -- the monolith [0, 100) is frozen

select is(pgpm.regrain_history('public.r8', '50'), 2, 'LIVENESS: first pass: the monolith split into two 50-wide children');
select is(pgpm.regrain_history('public.r8'), 5, 'LIVENESS: second pass: the oldest 50-wide child split into 10-wide children');
select ok(exists (select 1 from pgpm.part where parent_table = 'public.r8'::regclass and attached and lo = '50' and hi = '100'),
  'LIVENESS: the coarse child [50, 100) is still attached');
select ok(exists (select 1 from pgpm.part where parent_table = 'public.r8'::regclass and attached and lo = '0' and hi = '10'),
  'LIVENESS: the smallest-lo attached child [0, 10) is already at the partition step');

select lives_ok($$ select pgpm.regrain_history('public.r8') $$,
  'regrain_history at the partition step regrains the remaining coarse child rather than refusing on a fine one');
select ok(not exists (select 1 from pgpm.part where parent_table = 'public.r8'::regclass and attached
                       and lo::bigint < 100 and hi::bigint - lo::bigint > 10),
  'no coarse child is left below the frontier');
select * from finish();
```

Acceptance: the reproduction(s) above fail on 60f4ad89 and must pass on the fixing commit; the fix carries a bench/ guard and a bench/mutations entry proven by ./test.sh discriminate.

Tier: 3

Found in adversarial review pass pass-1 reconciliation (lever-12) at `60f4ad89`, root-cause group LP3: P1F-06.

## P1F-06

- finder: P1F
- location: `pgpm_core/install.sql:1428`
- lens: pass-1 reconciliation
- tier: 3
- scenario: transmute accepts p_regrain_batch => 0 (or negative) and records it; regrain_step clamps it to 1, so auto-regrain copies one row per tick for good, where it should refuse it up front as it refuses p_obtain < 0 (pass-1 T14)
- root cause (verifier): transmute validates p_obtain (#581, _refuse_bad_transmute_arguments) but not p_regrain_batch: 0 or a negative value is accepted and recorded in pgpm.config.regrain_batch (no setter changes it afterwards), and regrain_step clamps it to greatest(1, batch) = 1, so every auto-regrain tick copies one row (maintain reports regrain=copied:1) instead of being refused up front. p_obtain < 0 is fixed (#581, PR #618); p_lock_timeout '0' fell: the reference accepts 'any lock_timeout value' (reference.md:380).

Reproduction: `repro.sql`, the finder's, run unchanged by the verifier.

```sql
-- P1F-06 (pass-1 T14): p_obtain < 0, p_regrain_batch = 0 and p_lock_timeout = '0' are accepted by transmute.
-- p_obtain < 0 is refused since #581; p_lock_timeout '0' is a lock_timeout value the reference accepts
-- ("any lock_timeout value"), so neither is asserted as the defect beyond the p_obtain refusal staying put.
-- p_regrain_batch => 0 (or a negative value) is accepted and recorded in pgpm.config.regrain_batch, which no
-- setter changes afterwards; regrain_step clamps it to greatest(1, 0) = 1, so every auto-regrain tick copies
-- ONE row (maintain logs regrain=copied:1). Present when transmute does not refuse a non-positive batch.
create extension if not exists pgtap;
set client_min_messages = warning;
select plan(4);

create table public.p1f06_o (id bigint primary key, v int);
insert into public.p1f06_o select g, g from generate_series(1, 250) g;
select throws_like($$call pgpm.transmute('public.p1f06_o', 'id', 100, p_obtain => -1, p_paused => false)$$,
  '%p_obtain must be a non-negative integer%', 'p_obtain => -1 is refused, as set_obtain refuses it');

-- a twin table proves the call shape converts when the batch is positive
create table public.p1f06_ok (id bigint primary key, v int);
insert into public.p1f06_ok select g, g from generate_series(1, 250) g;
call pgpm.transmute('public.p1f06_ok', 'id', 100, p_obtain => 3, p_paused => false, p_regrain_batch => 5000);
select is((select regrain_batch from pgpm.config where parent_table = 'public.p1f06_ok'::regclass), 5000,
  'LIVENESS: the same call with a positive batch converts and records it');

create table public.p1f06_z (id bigint primary key, v int);
insert into public.p1f06_z select g, g from generate_series(1, 250) g;
select throws_ok($$call pgpm.transmute('public.p1f06_z', 'id', 100, p_obtain => 3, p_paused => false, p_regrain_batch => 0)$$,
  'P0001', NULL, 'p_regrain_batch => 0 is refused up front (not run into its first COMMIT)');
create table public.p1f06_m (id bigint primary key, v int);
insert into public.p1f06_m select g, g from generate_series(1, 250) g;
select throws_ok($$call pgpm.transmute('public.p1f06_m', 'id', 100, p_obtain => 3, p_paused => false, p_regrain_batch => -5)$$,
  'P0001', NULL, 'p_regrain_batch => -5 is refused up front');
select * from finish();
```

Acceptance: the reproduction(s) above fail on 60f4ad89 and must pass on the fixing commit; the fix carries a bench/ guard and a bench/mutations entry proven by ./test.sh discriminate.

