Found in adversarial review pass pass-1 reconciliation (lever-12) at `60f4ad89`, root-cause group LP2: P1H-02.

## P1H-02

- finder: P1H
- location: `pgpm_core/install.sql:3036`
- lens: contract
- tier: 3
- scenario: pass-1 A7: extend_to's p_max dry count walks grid steps from the data frontier (max(id)), counting the obtain lookahead's existing partitions too, so a call that would create 2 new partitions is refused under p_max => 3 with 'would need more than 3 new partitions'; reference.md says p_max bounds how many NEW partitions one call may create
- root cause (verifier): extend_to's dry count walks grid steps from the floor of the DATA frontier (_frontier_native = max(control) on an id grid), counting the partitions obtain's lookahead already built as new, so a call creating 2 partitions is refused under p_max => 3 with the false text 'would need more than 3 new partitions'; docs/reference.md and docs/guide.md:461 say p_max bounds how many NEW partitions one call may create (the in-code comment calls the overcount a deliberate conservative bound, but neither operator document nor the error text says so, and the lookahead inflates it by config.obtain)

Reproduction: `repro.sql`, the finder's, run unchanged by the verifier.

```sql
-- P1H-02 (pass-1 A7): docs/reference.md (extend_to): "`p_max` bounds how many NEW partitions one call may
-- create". The dry count walks grid steps from the floor of the DATA frontier (max(id) on an id grid), so the
-- partitions obtain's lookahead already built between max(id) and the forward edge are counted as new. Here
-- the call needs two new partitions ([400,500) and [500,600)) and is refused under p_max => 3 with "would need
-- more than 3 new partitions".
create extension if not exists pgtap;
set client_min_messages = warning;
select plan(6);

create table public.p1h02_ev (id bigint primary key, payload text);
insert into public.p1h02_ev values (7, 'a'), (42, 'b'), (88, 'c');
call pgpm.transmute('public.p1h02_ev', 'id', 100, p_obtain => 3);

select is((select max(hi::numeric) from pgpm.part where parent_table = 'public.p1h02_ev'::regclass), 400::numeric,
  'LIVENESS: the obtain lookahead built the grid up to 400, past the data frontier');
select is((select max(id) from public.p1h02_ev), 88::bigint, 'LIVENESS: the data frontier is 88');
select ok(not exists (select 1 from pgpm.part where parent_table = 'public.p1h02_ev'::regclass and hi::numeric > 400),
  'LIVENESS: nothing exists past 400, so reaching 550 takes exactly two new partitions');

select lives_ok($$select pgpm.extend_to('public.p1h02_ev', '550', 3)$$,
  'extend_to accepts a call that creates 2 new partitions under p_max => 3');
select is(array(select lo from pgpm.part where parent_table = 'public.p1h02_ev'::regclass and lo::numeric >= 400 order by lo::numeric),
  array['400', '500'], 'it built [400,500) and [500,600)');
select is(pgpm.extend_to('public.p1h02_ev', '550', 1), 0, 'a repeat call creates nothing and is not refused under p_max => 1');
select * from finish();
```

Acceptance: the reproduction(s) above fail on 60f4ad89 and must pass on the fixing commit; the fix carries a bench/ guard and a bench/mutations entry proven by ./test.sh discriminate.

